.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt PASSWD 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm passwd ,
.Nm master.passwd
.Nd the account database
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The file
.Pa /etc/master.passwd ,
readable only by the superuser, holds one line per account with ten
fields separated by colons:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
name:password:uid:gid:class:change:expire:gecos:home:shell
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width password
.It Ar name
The login name.
.It Ar password
The
.Xr crypt 3
hash of the password.
Empty means no password is needed; a hash beginning with
.Ql \&*
or
.Ql \&!
locks the account.
.It Ar uid , Ar gid
The user and primary group IDs.
.It Ar class
The login class in
.Xr login.conf 5 .
.It Ar change
The time, in seconds since the Epoch, by which the password must be
changed; 0 for none.
.It Ar expire
The time, in seconds since the Epoch, at which the account expires; 0 for
none.
.It Ar gecos
The user's full name and similar information.
.It Ar home
The home directory.
.It Ar shell
The login shell; empty means
.Pa /bin/sh .
.El
.Pp
The public
.Pa /etc/passwd ,
readable by everyone, is generated from it by
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8 .
It has seven fields, with the password replaced by
.Ql *
and the class, change and expire fields left out:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
name:*:uid:gid:gecos:home:shell
.Ed
.Pp
There is no
.Pa /etc/shadow .
The C library's
.Xr getspnam 3
reads
.Pa /etc/master.passwd ,
reporting the change time as the day the password was last changed with
a maximum age of 0, and the expire time as the account's expiry day.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/master.passwd -compact
.It Pa /etc/master.passwd
.It Pa /etc/passwd
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr crypt 3 ,
.Xr getpwent 3 ,
.Xr login.conf 5 ,
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
file format appeared in
.At v1 .
.Pa master.passwd
appeared in
.Bx 4.3 Reno .
